*  FORTREAD_driver - exercises FORTREAD().  Contract per FORTREAD.sno header:
*  FORTREAD() reads in and returns the next FORTRAN statement on the input
*  stream -- so comment lines (C in column 1) are skipped and continuation
*  lines (a nonblank in column 6) are joined onto the statement they continue.
*  It fails at end of input.  The FORTRAN deck is FORTREAD_driver.input.
-INCLUDE "FORTREAD.sno"
LOOP    S  =  FORTREAD()                                :F(DONE)
        OUTPUT  =  '[' S ']'                            :(LOOP)
DONE    OUTPUT  =  'end of deck'
END
